>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must be 1-D or 2-D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 2
>>
Rule 2 (diagonal value is within a reasonable range based on input dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then v_2 ≥ (0 - (shape(v_1, 0) - 1)) ∧ v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 0) - 1 else if ndim(v_1) = 2 then v_2 ≥ (0 - (shape(v_1, 0) - 1)) ∧ v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 1) - 1 else false
>>
Rule 3 (If input is 1D, one dimension of the output shape should be equal to input size)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then ∃i ∈ [0, 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_1, 0)
